\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  Now the day is over
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Night is drawing nigh,
\par Shadows of the evening
\par Steal across the sky.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2. Now the darkness gathers,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Stars begin to peep,
\par  Birds, and beasts, and flowers
\par Soon will be asleep
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  3. Jesus, give the weary
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Calm and sweet repose;
\par  With Thy tender blessing
\par  May mine eyelids close.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  4. Grant to little children
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Visions bright of Thee;
\par Guard the sailors tossing
\par On the deep blue sea.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-315\li450\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par   5.  Comfort every sufferer
\par \pard\li450\sl190\slmult0 Watching late in pain;
\par Those who plan some evil
\par From their sin restrain.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-315\li450\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par   6.  Through the long night-watches,
\par \pard\li450\sl190\slmult0 May Thine angels spread
\par Their white wings above me,
\par Watching round my bed
\par 
\par \pard\fi-315\li450\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par   7.  When the morning wakens,
\par \pard\li450\sl190\slmult0 Then may I arise
\par Pure, and fresh, and sinless
\par In Thy holy eyes.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li450\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  8. Glory to the Father,
\par \pard\li450\sl190\slmult0  Glory to the Son,
\par And to Thee, blest Spirit,
\par \pard        Whilst all ages run.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

